          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em generalized homology theory
            is a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            from suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+abelian+groups"} graded abelian groups
            which satisfies most, but not all, of the abstract properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
            functors (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is the coefficient object of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spanier-Whitehead+duality"} S-dually
            of a generalized homology theory. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                  %mi H
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = H R
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
            this reduces to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} ordinary homology
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            for more.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#reduced_homology Reduced homology
          %p
            Throughout, write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi CW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_{CW}
            for the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}_{CW}
            for the corresponding category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
          %p
            Recall that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
            are computed as colimits in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            after adjoining the base point and its inclusion maps to the given diagram
          #WedgeSumAsCoproduct.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∨
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee_{i \in I} X_i
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma \coloneqq S^1 \wedge (-)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Top^{\ast/}_{CW} \longrightarrow Top^{\ast/}_{CW}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+suspension"} reduced suspension
            functor.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ab
                    %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab^{\mathbb{Z}}
            for the category of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+abelian+groups"} graded abelian groups
          #ReducedGeneralizedHomology.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong reduced homology theory
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi CW
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi Ab
                      %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde E_\bullet
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (Top^{\ast/}_{CW}) \longrightarrow Ab^{\mathbb{Z}}
            %p
              from the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"}> CW-complexes
              ) to
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+abelian+groups"} graded abelian groups
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+groups"}> homology groups
              ”), in components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde E _\bullet
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (X \stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow} Y)
                    \\mapsto
                    (\tilde E_\bullet(X)
                    \\stackrel{f_\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\tilde E_\bullet(Y))
                    \\,,
            %p
              and equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              of degree +1, to be called the
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+isomorphism"} suspension isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\tilde E_\bullet(-)
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\tilde E_{\bullet +1}(\Sigma -)
            %p such that:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+invariance"}> homotopy invariance
                    )
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1,f_2 \colon X \longrightarrow Y
                  are two morphisms of pointed topological spaces such that there is a (base point preserving)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1 \simeq f_2
                  between them, then the induced
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
                  of abelian groups are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equal
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mo
                          %mo *
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mo
                          %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f_1_\ast = f_2_\ast
                        \\,.
              %li#ReducedExactnessAxiom
                %p
                  %strong (exactness)
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon A \hookrightarrow X
                  an inclusion of pointed topological spaces, with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Cone
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \colon X \longrightarrow Cone(i)
                  the induced
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
                  of graded abelian groups
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi j
                              %mo *
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Cone
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\tilde E_\bullet(A)
                        \\overset{i_\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                        \\tilde E_\bullet(X)
                        \\overset{j_\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                        \\tilde E_\bullet(Cone(i))
                        \\,.
            %p
              We say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E_\bullet
              is
              %strong additive
              if in addition
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+axiom"}> wedge axiom
                    )
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X_i\}_{i \in I}
                  any set of pointed CW-complexes, then the canonical morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mo ∨
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\oplus_{i \in I} \tilde E_\bullet(X_i)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\tilde E^\bullet(\vee_{i \in I} X_i)
                %p
                  from the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                  of the value on the summands to the value on the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WedgeSumAsCoproduct"}
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              We say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E_\bullet
              is
              %strong ordinary
              if its value on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0
              is concentrated in degree 0:
            %ul
              %li
                %strong (Dimension)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ≠
                            %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E_{\bullet\neq 0}(\mathbb{S}^0) \simeq 0
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of reduced cohomology theories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta \;\colon\; \tilde E_\bullet \longrightarrow \tilde F_\bullet
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              between the underlying functors which is compatible with the suspension isomorphisms in that all the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} squares commute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi F
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi Σ
                                    %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\tilde E_\bullet(X) &amp;\overset{\eta_X}{\longrightarrow}&amp;  \tilde F_\bullet(X)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\sigma_E}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\sigma_F}}
                    \\\
                    \\tilde E_{\bullet + 1}(\Sigma X)
                    \&amp;\overset{\eta_{\Sigma X}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\tilde F_{\bullet + 1}(\Sigma X)
                    }
                    \\,.
          %h3#unreduced_homology Unreduced homology
          %p
            In the following a
            %em pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,A)
            refers to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"}> CW-complexes
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \emptyset)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                    %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{CW}^{\hookrightarrow}
            for the category of such pairs (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{CW}
            on the inclusions). We identify
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                  %mo ↪
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                    %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{CW} \hookrightarrow Top_{CW}^{\hookrightarrow}
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto (X,\emptyset)
          #GeneralizedHomologyTheory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong homology theory
              (unreduced,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cohomology"} relative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi CW
                      %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi Ab
                      %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E_\bullet : (Top_{CW}^{\hookrightarrow}) \longrightarrow Ab^{\mathbb{Z}}
            %p
              to the category of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+abelian+groups"} graded abelian groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              of degree +1, to be called the
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphism"} connecting homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_{(X,A)}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    E_{\bullet + 1}(X, A)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    E_\bullet(A, \emptyset)
                    \\,.
            %p such that:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong (homotopy invariance)
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon (X_1,A_1) \to (X_2,A_2)
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
                  of pairs, then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        E_\bullet(f)
                        \\;\colon\;
                        E_\bullet(X_1,A_1) \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} E_\bullet(X_2,A_2)
                %p
                  is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %li#ExactnessUnreduced
                %p
                  %strong (exactness)
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
                  the induced sequence
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi δ
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi ⋯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\cdots
                        \\to
                        E_{n+1}(X, A)
                        \\stackrel{\delta}{\longrightarrow}
                        E_n(A)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        E_n(X)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        E_n(X, A)
                        \\to
                        \\cdots
                %p
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              %li#excision
                %p
                  %strong
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excision"}> excision
                    )
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow A \hookrightarrow X
                  such that
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mover
                            %mi U
                            %mo ¯
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi Int
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{U} \subset Int(A)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo −
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo −
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon (X-U, A-U) \hookrightarrow (X, A)
                  induces an isomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo −
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo −
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        E_\bullet(i)
                        \\;\colon\;
                        E_n(X-U, A-U)
                        \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                        E_n(X, A)
            %p
              We say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet
              is
              %strong additive
              if it takes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              to
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %strong (additivity)
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, A) = \coprod_i (X_i, A_i)
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\oplus_i E_n(X_i, A_i) \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} E_n(X, A)
                %p
                  is an
                  = succeed "from" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                  of the value on the summands, to the value on the total pair.
            %p
              We say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet
              is
              %strong ordinary
              if its value on the point is concentrated in degree 0
            %ul
              %li
                %strong> (Dimension)
                \:
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ≠
                            %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{\bullet \neq 0}(\ast,\emptyset) = 0
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of unreduced homology theories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta \;\colon\; E_\bullet \longrightarrow F_\bullet
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              of the underlying functors that is compatible with the connecting homomorphisms, hence such that all these
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} squares commute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi A
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mi F
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ∅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi A
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi ∅
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ∅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    E_{\bullet +1}(X,A)
                    \&amp;\overset{\eta_{(X,A)}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    F_{\bullet +1}(X,A)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\delta_E}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\delta_F}}
                    \\\
                    E_\bullet(A,\emptyset) &amp;\overset{\eta_{(A,\emptyset)}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; F_\bullet(A,\emptyset)
                    }
                    \\,.
          #AlternativeFormulationOfExcisionAxiom.num_defn
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              The excision axiom in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralizedHomologyTheory"}
              is equivalent to the following statement:
            %p
              For all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \hookrightarrow X
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = A \cup B
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i \colon (A, A \cap B) \longrightarrow (X,B)
            %p induces an isomorphism,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i_\ast
                    \\;\colon\;
                    E_\bullet(A, A \cap B)
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    E_\bullet(X, B)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Switzer75"} Switzer 75, 7.2, 7.5
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              First consider the statement under the condition that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Int(A) \cup Int(B)
            %p
              In one direction, suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              satisfies the original excision axiom. Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \Int(A) \cup Int(B)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \coloneqq X-A
              and observe that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi U
                              %mo ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mo −
                                %mi A
                              %mo ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi X
                            %mo −
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\overline{U}
                    \&amp; = \overline{X-A}
                    \\\ &amp; = X- Int(A)
                    \\\ &amp; \subset Int(B)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p and that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X-U, B-U) = (A, A \cap B)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence the excision axiom implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet(X, B) \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} E^\bullet(A, A \cap B)
            %p
              Conversely, suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              satisfies the alternative condition. Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow A \hookrightarrow X
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi U
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{U} \subset Int(A)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo −
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∪
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo −
                            %mover
                              %mi U
                              %mo ¯
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∩
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⊃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo −
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Int(X-U) \cup Int(A)
                    \&amp; = (X - \overline{U}) \cap \Int(A)
                    \\\ &amp; \supset (X - Int(A)) \cap Int(A)
                    \\\ &amp; = X
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p and that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X-U, (X-U) \cap A) = (X-U, A - U)
                    \\,.
            %p Hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^\bullet(X-U,A-U)
                    \\simeq
                    E^\bullet(X-U, (X-U)\cap A)
                    \\simeq
                    E^\bullet(X,A)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This shows the statement for the special case that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Int(A)\cup Int(U)
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Switzer75"} Switzer 75, 7.5
          #ExactSequenceOfATriple.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (exact sequence of a triple)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet
              an unreduced generalized cohomology theory, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralizedHomologyTheory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z \hookrightarrow Y \hookrightarrow X
            %p
              induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
              of homology groups of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mover
                        %mi δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\to
                    E_q(Y,Z)
                    \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                    E_q(X,Z)
                    \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                    E_q(X,Y)
                    \\stackrel{\bar \delta}{\longrightarrow}
                    E_{q-1}(Y,Z)
                    \\to
                    \\cdots
            %p where
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar \delta
                    \\;\colon \;
                    E_{q}(X,Y)
                    \\stackrel{\delta}{\longrightarrow}
                    E_{q-1}(Y)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    E_{q-1}(Y,Z)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Apply the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+lemma"} braid lemma
              to the interlocking long exact sequences of the three pairs
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,Y)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,Z)
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,Z)
            %p
              %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BraidDiagramForHomologyOnTripled.jpg", :width => "500"}/
            %p
              (graphics from
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.stackexchange.com/a/1180681/58526"} this Maths.SE comment
            %p
              See
              %a{:href => "braid+lemma#ExactSequenceForTripleInGeneralizedHomology"} here
              for details.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#expression_by_ordinary_homology_via_atiyahhirzebruch_spectral_sequence Expression by ordinary homology via Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hirzebruch+spectral+sequence"} Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence
            serves to express generalized homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet
            in terms of ordinary homology with coefficients in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet(\ast)
          %h3#WhiteheadTheorem Whitehead theorem
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon E \longrightarrow F
              be a morphism of reduced generalized (co-)homology functors, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedHomology"}
              (a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi(S^0) \colon E(S^0) \longrightarrow F(S^0)
            %p
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(X)\colon E(X)\to F(X)
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              of cells. If both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              satisfy the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+axiom"} wedge axiom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(X)
              is an isomorphism for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
            functors a proof of this is in (
            %a{:href => "#EilenbergSteenrod52"}> Eilenberg-Steenrod 52, section III.10
            ). From this the general statement follows (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Kochman96"} Kochman 96, theorem 3.4.3, corollary 4.2.8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hirzebruch+spectral+sequence"} Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence
            (the classical result gives that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            induces an isomorphism between the second pages of the AHSSs for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Switzer75"} Switzer 75, theorem 7.55, theorem 7.67
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+homology+theory"} stable homotopy homology theory
                is the homology theory represented by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
                is the homology theory represented by an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+homology+theory"} bordism homology theory
                is the homology theory represented by a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
